1. Which major ecological domains currently have the largest monitoring gaps?
2. Which federal datasets are most difficult to integrate?
3. Where do state monitoring systems lack national comparability?
4. Which information systems have the strongest demonstrated connections to management outcomes?
5. Which monitoring programs provide the greatest value per dollar?
6. Where are long-term monitoring records at risk of discontinuation?
7. Which ecological indicators provide the strongest early-warning capability?
8. How frequently does monitoring actually trigger management changes?
9. Where are biological outcomes inadequately measured?
10. Which datasets are redundant?
11. Which datasets are uniquely valuable?
12. What information is collected but rarely used?
13. Where does data quality prevent reliable inference?
14. What common identifiers would generate the greatest interoperability benefits?
